# Line endings and byte-order marks.
#
# install.sh acquired a UTF-8 BOM from a Windows editor, which made its
# shebang unrunnable:
#
#     install.sh: line 1: ﻿#!/bin/bash: No such file or directory
#
# The script still limped along under 'bash install.sh', so the breakage
# showed up only as a puzzling first line in otherwise normal output - and
# a .con file caught the same way fails on its first directive with a
# message about a keyword that looks perfectly correct on screen.
#
# Normalise to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except the vendor drops, which are not ours to reformat and include
# binaries that must not be touched.
libs/TUCamSample_*/** -text
libs/vendor/** -text
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.so binary
*.d binary
